  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 900 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nThe beginning of the long term period will be categorized by \nupper ridging over the Southeast, keeping seasonably warm and dry \nconditions in place over the region. High temps will range from \nthe low to mid 70s with what should be plenty of sunshine through \nthe day. Like recent days, we will have to monitor dewpoint \ndepressions in case RHs drop to a level that would be more \ncritical for fire conditions, but light winds will mitigate larger\nfire concerns. The mid to lake week period gets a bit more \nuncertain as a series of upper waves are progged to traverse to \nour north around the Great Lakes region, pushing cold fronts \nthrough the northern Plains and Midwest. For now it does not look \nlike these systems will amplify enough to dig this far south, but \nwe will continue to monitor trends. For now, we will maintain a \ndry forecast with daily highs in the 70s and lows in the 40s to \nlower 50s.",
